WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.451
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.710
 Hey Marvel fans, I'm
Ryan Penagos, a.k.a.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.260
Agent M, and I'm so
excited to be sitting here

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.780
with VFX supervisor
of Marvel Studios

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.240
Avengers: Endgame, Dan DeLeeuw.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.070
How are you doing, Dan?

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:26.930
 Doing great.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.020
 So there's so much to
talk about in this film.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.570
You worked three years on it.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.450
I-- let's just dive
right into some stuff.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.250
You ready?

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.050
 Yep.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:36.950
Lets' go.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.120
RYAN PENAGOS: You know I
think about this big battle,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.120
how much creative input
do you have in seeing

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.410
all this come together?

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.577
DAN DELEEUW: You
know, you get kind

00:00:46.577 --> 00:00:48.470
of a rough idea of what
the story needs to be,

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.090
get a rough idea
from Joe and Anthony.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.220
It's like, OK, these are
the beats we want to do,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.510
we want the compound to blow
up, we want to make a crater.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.030
This is kind of where
the dreams come true,

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.100
you know, in terms
of growing up,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.680
loving comics, loving
films, and then

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.160
getting to design these fights.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.050
I kind of describe it as you
had your little action figures

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.110
you had when you were a kid.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.180
And now like, you're grown up.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.830
You're doing the same
things with real people

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.760
and stunties and CG characters.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.610
And you kind of sit down
and start brainstorming.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:19.010
It's like, what has to happen?

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.740
And it's like Cap's
going to pick up Mjolnir.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.850
He's going to take up--

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.055
he's going to pick up the
hammer, one way or another.

00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:27.390
If it's the last thing I do,
he's picking up that hammer.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.090
 Assemble.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.800
RYAN PENAGOS: So you
get to the moment

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.960
where the portals
start opening up.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.760
How many layers are going
on in a shot like that?

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:41.700
 It's pretty--

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.780
I mean, astronomical is a kind
of an easy way to describe it.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.120
We had our big days where
we had everybody there.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.950
You kind of see it
in the big masters,

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.620
and when Cap says assemble,
everybody's standing there

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.790
and we had all
the actors on set.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.250
And then depending
on who we had,

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.940
it dictated what would be
CG and what wouldn't be.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:02.810
We had like a dirt floor, we
had some wreckage and rubble,

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.450
and some of that we would
replace, depending on if it

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.170
made it easier to light
the shot or the composition

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:07.970
would get better.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.330
But when you get into
the portals opening up,

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.500
you've got everybody on this
side of the portals with the CG

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.870
crater, CG fire, CG smoke,
CG atmosphere, CG embers, CG

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.560
dust, CG ash floating around.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.200
And then you've got
the portals themselves,

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.060
which they're their
own effect simulation,

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.890
complex effects simulation.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:30.890
And then you've got all
the "digis" walking out.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.090
We just didn't want
to make it feel

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.280
like they're coming from
kind of this flat space

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.080
when you see the portal.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.570
You wanted it to feel like
it's a dimensional space.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:42.980
With Marvel, too, it is a shared
universe, everything's online.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.070
Everything's in the archives.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.800
So if you need to go
back and get Contraxia,

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.320
you just go back
and get Contraxia.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.470
 That's so cool.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.390
 It's just there, right, so--

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.150
and then we had Andy Thy
built portions of New Asgard,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.370
so we did portions
of New Asgard.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:57.650
So it's like you've got
everything in this world,

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.277
and plus everything from
all the other worlds

00:02:59.277 --> 00:03:00.110
that they're coming from.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.260
So it's almost incalculable
in terms of how much we have.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.168
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:04.168 --> 00:03:05.530
 Is that everyone?

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.030
 What, you want even more?

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.070
RYAN PENAGOS: We then
get into the battle.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:13.390
You've got that wonderful
scene, Cap rallying everyone,

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:16.030
he assembles everyone,
charge, and you

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.990
have a lot of actual, physical,
practical people and effects

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:21.790
and stuff.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:26.050
They are charging into
just hordes of enemies.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.727
But those are all VFX, right?

00:03:27.727 --> 00:03:29.460
DAN DELEEUW: Yeah, no, the
before and after of those

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.230
are the best before
and afters ever,

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.790
in terms of just
the work that we did

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.000
and just the general
comedy of what

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.000
was actually happening on set.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:36.800
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.320
So if you look at
the shots and there's

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.550
the shot where we
begin kind the one

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:43.900
where you come in,
right, when Giant

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.070
Man punches the Leviathan.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.420
But you're zooming in
on that, you've got

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:48.710
all the heroes running forward.

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.620
And you've got your actors
there and then there's

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:55.030
maybe like six guys in motion
capture suits running at them,

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.167
again, just to kind
of let all the actors

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.300
know, generally,
where the eyeline

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.530
is for the approaching aliens.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:04.000
But yeah, Thanos's army was
kind of weak in that version

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:04.800
of the show.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.120
 He just came with six.
DAN DELEEUW: Yeah,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:06.920
 Oh no.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:07.870
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.670
DAN DELEEUW: Yeah, it's
sometimes the befores are just

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.310
some of the oddly
crude things, but it

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:13.670
was something that worked.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.470
It got them there.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.860
It was like, we were hooking it
up, we had the kind of big shot

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.569
where you kind of went into
the live action of everybody

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:21.510
running together.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.740
Then you comes up into the
air to see Giant Man punch

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.420
Leviathan, you go
back to CG, and then

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.220
you come back down again on
Panther and Okoye and Shuri.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.960
And that was shot as a separate
little piece on their set.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.730
And then as you pan left,
you get a little bit

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.940
of a CG Drax coming in
that pulls you from that,

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.350
that lands into the live
action Dave Bautista, who's

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.500
on this kind of, I don't
know, large punching bag

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.450
thing with stunt guys
hanging all over it,

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.863
trying to make sure Dave
didn't fall off of it.

00:04:45.863 --> 00:04:47.530
 And then there's, you
know, the guy in the mocap

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.060
suit for Korg, which,
just, all of it,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.580
it's this elegant ballet.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.170
And it's really neat.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.770
All right, last but not least,
we have to talk about one

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.740
of the moments that made
crowds roar, that gives

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:00.820
you all the biggest feels.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.760
It's when we see all the
women of Marvel come together.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.590
They're on the battlefield.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.750
How much of that was
filmed practically,

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:12.170
how much was added in, and how
do you bring that all together?

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.330
 Well we had everyone there.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.970
There was like two or three
weeks where everybody is there.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:20.170
You've got every
Avenger from every movie

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.820
that we've done all on
set at the same time.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.140
And so it was a great
day to go to set,

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:30.250
because it's like, whoa,
there's Pepper, there's Okoye,

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.090
there's Valkyrie.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.130
There's like all the
characters you love

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.060
are actually there on set.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.060
So when they all come
together, the idea

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.680
of having this kind of
passing of the torch,

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.230
passing the gauntlet, there was
a lot of symbolism going on.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.490
But then it was
also something that

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.990
was kind of special to do, to
bring all the women of Marvel

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:45.790
together.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.760
So when we shot it, you
had everybody there.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.330
Valkyrie, we put in, later, a
different element, because she

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.890
was on the back of the Pegasus.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.710
 You didn't have a
practical Pegasus for this?

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.750
 We tried, but again, that's
probably like three years out.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.580
Cloning's two
years, three years.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.130
But anyway, you know,
she's landing in the back.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.940
For the most part, we
had everybody there.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:08.080
And so we go ahead
and shot him, you

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.440
pull them, you'll add Pepper's
armor later, you'll have--

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.980
Hope comes in as
the Wasp and grows,

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:19.060
so you actually have
Evangeline there kind

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.270
of walking in the shot,
and you just kind of

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.370
paint her out and
then just kind of have

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.080
the Wasp grow into her size.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.500
 I was sitting in a
crowd opening night

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.630
and I watched a
kid in front of me

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:37.110
jump up out of his chair,
arms up in the air, scream,

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.410
everybody's like crying
and laughing and cheering.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.990
How much fun is it for you
guys to put all this together

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.420
and then to see it work?

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.690
 It's the best part.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.330
You know, it's the--

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.100
we're all fans too, right.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.520
So then there's all these
moments that you want to see.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.340
And then for us, it's something
that you see it in previs

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.950
and you're kind of like,
OK, that's really cool.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:58.950
It's going to be really great.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.510
And so you see all
these scenes in pieces

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.580
and you see them kind of
come together in editorial.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.550
And I remember the first
time we kind of cut

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.490
the portals together,
and Jeff Ward called

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.610
me and he said, take a look.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.673
And it's like, you a little
tear in the corner of your eye.

00:07:11.673 --> 00:07:13.140
And then you're kind
of like, this is great.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.990
This is going to work.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.995
And then part of the
fun is then going in

00:07:16.995 --> 00:07:18.810
to see with the real audience
and just kind of see,

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.927
OK, is this going to work?

00:07:21.927 --> 00:07:23.160
You're sitting there
and you're like,

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.470
oh my god, this totally works.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.310
[LAUGHTER]

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.880
You go opening weekend
and then people

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.020
are just going nuts over it.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.900
And I think that's the
best part, the most

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.810
rewarding part, that
everybody loved what we did,

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:34.680
which is great.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.780
 Dan, thanks so much
for sharing so much

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.030
about Marvel Studio's
Avengers: Endgame.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.600
You guys, make sure you
pick up the film now.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.750
[MUSIC PLAYING]

